        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (3), by substituting for the words \"Juvenile Courts Act 1947\" the words \"Child Act 2001\". Amendment of section 294"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_17",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "17",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 294(1) of the Code is amended by substituting for the words \"not being a youthful offender has been convicted of any offence punishable with imprisonment\" the words \"has been convicted of any offence\". Amendment of section 295"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_18",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "18",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 295 of the Code is amended by inserting after subsection (1) the following subsection: \" (1A) When a person is convicted of an offence under section 376, 377c or 377E of the Penal Code before any Court, the Court shall direct that he be subject to the supervision of the police for a period of not less than one year and not more than three years commencing immediately after the expiration of the sentence passed on him.\". Amendment of section 307"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_19",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "19",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 307 of the Code is amended in subsections (1) and (4) and paragraph (5)(b) by substituting for the word \"ten\" the word \"fourteen\". Amendment of First Schedule"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act may be cited as the Criminal Procedure Code (Amendment) Act 2004."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act comes into operation on a date to be appointed by the Minister by notification in the Gazette, and the Minister may appoint different dates for the coming into operation of different provisions of this Act. Amendment of section 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_2",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Criminal Procedure Code [Act 593], which is referred to as the \"Code\" in this Act, is amended in subsection 2(1) by substituting for the definition of \"youthful offender\" the following definition: ' \" youthful offender\" means a person convicted of an offence punishable by fine or imprisonment who is of or above the age of eighteen and below the age of 21;'. Amendment of section 10"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2004/16/eng@/~cl_20",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "20",
